\textcolor{blue}{The constellation contains 180 satellites and follows the slot based topology model in Sec.~\ref{sec:sys_model}.
Each microservice is associated with a CPU cycle demand, an image size, and a storage requirement.}
\textcolor{blue}{Satellite CPUs are heterogeneous. To represent concurrent tasks that are not explicitly instantiated as target requests, every satellite has a background computation state and every ISL has a background traffic state. Each state evolves across slots according to a Markov chain with finitely many states. The sampled computation state determines the effective processing rate and background computation queue, while the sampled traffic state determines the effective ISL rate and background transmission queue. These Markov processes are the only source of resource contention external to the target requests.}
Requests invoke sequential microservice chains.
\textcolor{blue}{The workload traces cover chain lengths of 5, 10, and 15 and are used consistently across the compared methods when requests are analyzed.}

